@@ -2,6 +2,20 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+### Changed
+
+- Expose a closed, branch-aligned partition of legacy and HT20 OFDM rejection
+  events across serial, parallel, and windowed Wi-Fi decoders, including an
+  explicit strong-path long-training timeout that may coexist with
+  weak-short-period recovery.
+- Subpartition that strong-path timeout by the furthest eligible acquisition
+  gate reached: no long-training evaluation, repeat, known-reference, or source
+  coordinates.
+- Probe repeated OFDM long-training windows whose reference score falls just
+  below the unchanged strong acceptance gate as bounded, lower-priority
+  hypotheses while retaining the original strong search and all SIGNAL, DATA,
+  and FCS integrity gates.
+
